  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 840 PM CDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\nThe main talking point in the long term will be monitoring the\nprogression of the aforementioned low pressure system as it shifts\nnortheastward out of the area. Ensembles have the Tennessee Valley\nremaining ahead of an upper level ridge to the west, supporting dry\nconditions through Tuesday. Depending on the progression of these\nsystems, the end of the long term could bring low chances of rainfall\nback into the forecast as early as Tuesday afternoon as the ridge\nprogresses east of our area. Confidence remains low in rain chances,\nso have continued with blended guidance for now. Otherwise, along\nwith the approaching ridge, a gradual warming pattern will be in\nstore for us. Highs are forecast to warm into the upper 80s to lower\n90s again Tuesday after being limited to the low to mid 80s through\nmost of the weekend. Lows are forecast to drop into the 50s through\nthe weekend, which will be a welcomed change after the above normal \npattern we've experienced the past several weeks. Don't break out the\nhot chocolate yet- the Climate Prediction Center continues to outlook\nthe Tennessee Valley in above normal temperatures through early\nOctober in the 8-14 day period. On the bright side, no heat products\nare on the horizon for us through at least the next 7 days.",
